{"title":"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An aquarium has a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangular</a> base that measures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> cm by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm and has a height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm. It is filled with water to a height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm. A brick with a rectangular base that measures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm and a height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm is placed in the aquarium. By how many centimeters does the water rise?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db692681787841bd9a2385dfde0be0d38771968c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 0.5 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 1.5 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 2.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"372\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The volume of the brick is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/2/372b417c76c252a8efd9c4230b6b9d9c5f999e7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40 \\times 20 \\times 10 = 8000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"158\" height=\"13\" />. Thus the water volume rose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/42197656595f6959a316a1841cb67815376d00f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8000 = 100 \\times 40 \\times h \\Longrightarrow h = 2\\ \\boxed{\\mathrm{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"291\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A\">2007 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/ind